<div class="editorial-grid">
  <section class="editorial-card">
    <h2>1. Respect for Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p>OnlinePDFPro respects the intellectual property rights of authors, educators, and publishers, and we expect users of our tools and study materials to do the same. We comply with the Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA) and applicable copyright laws worldwide.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-card">
    <h2>2. User-Processed Documents</h2>
    <p>OnlinePDFPro’s PDF and image utilities operate primarily inside the user’s own web browser. We do not host a public repository of user-uploaded files, nor do we inspect or claim ownership over documents processed by users through our tools.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-card">
    <h2>3. Free Study Materials for College Studies</h2>
    <p>All study materials published on OnlinePDFPro (including our chapter-wise DBMS Complete Notes PDF series) are original educational guides prepared for free college study and exam revision. Students may view and download these PDFs free of charge for personal academic use, but commercial redistribution or resale is strictly prohibited.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-card">
    <h2>4. How to Submit a Copyright / DMCA Takedown Notice</h2>
    <p>If you believe that any content hosted on OnlinePDFPro infringes your copyright, please send a written notice containing the following details:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Copyrighted Work:</strong> A clear description of the copyrighted work you claim has been infringed.</li>
      <li><strong>Location on OnlinePDFPro:</strong> The exact URL(s) on <code>onlinepdfpro.com</code> where the allegedly infringing material is located.</li>
      <li><strong>Contact Details:</strong> Your full name, mailing address, phone number, and email address.</li>
      <li><strong>Good-Faith Statement:</strong> A statement that you have a good-faith belief that the disputed use is not authorized by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law.</li>
      <li><strong>Verification &amp; Signature:</strong> A statement made under penalty of perjury that the information in your notice is accurate and that you are authorized to act on behalf of the copyright owner, accompanied by your electronic or physical signature.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-card">
    <h2>5. Designated Copyright Contact</h2>
    <p>Please send all copyright inquiries, DMCA takedown notices, or counter-notifications directly to:</p>
    <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@onlinepdfpro.com">support@onlinepdfpro.com</a><br><strong>Subject Line:</strong> Copyright / DMCA Notice — OnlinePDFPro</p>
